# =====================================================================
# ROOT IS AN ALLOW-LIST (2026-08-03, operator decision)
# =====================================================================
# Everything at the repo root is ignored, and the entries below are then
# re-admitted by name. A new file dropped in the root is therefore PRIVATE by
# default, and publishing it is a deliberate act — which is what the CLAUDE.md
# standing rule already claims happens ("assume any new file is public unless
# its directory is in that set").
#
# It previously worked the other way: ~24 rules each naming one specific file
# (`pppa-reply.docx`, `scripts/hunt_dombrava_20514.py`, ...). That protects the
# exact name and nothing else — rename the file, or drop a sibling next to it,
# and the protection is gone. The repo is PUBLIC and mirrors from this tree, so
# the deny-list put the burden on somebody remembering a rule every time.
#
# Adding a new top-level directory or root file? Add its `!` line here in the
# same commit, or git will not see it. That failure is loud (the file simply
# does not appear in `git status`), which is the intended direction: a missing
# allow rule costs a commit, a missing deny rule costs a disclosure.
#
# Deeper rules below still apply INSIDE these directories — `!/data/` re-admits
# the directory, it does not re-admit `data/*.json`.
/*

!/.claude/
!/.github/
!/assets/
!/backlog/
!/content/
!/curated/
!/data/
!/design/
!/docs/
!/scripts/
!/src/
!/templates/
!/tests/
!/wiki/

!/.env.deploy.example
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore
!/ARCHITECTURE.md
!/BACKLOG.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/pyproject.toml
!/requirements.lock
!/requirements.txt
!/serve.py
!/sources.yaml

# =====================================================================
# Rules that apply at ANY depth (inside the allowed directories above)
# =====================================================================

# Database
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
data/*.backup
data/*.backup-*
data/*.json
# VAD homonīmu deny-list — operator-kurēta konfigurācija, ko lasa src/vad/denylist.py.
# Jābūt versiju kontrolē: svaigā klonā trūkstošs fails nozīmētu klusi tukšus vārtus
# (un tests test_vad_denylist.py prasa, lai tas eksistē).
!data/vad_denylist.json
data/backups/

# Scratch output from routines (weekly skeleton md, saeima calendar snapshots).
# The former root-only entries here (/scratch_*, /scratchpad_*, /calendar.md,
# /eval_matcher_out.json, pppa-reply.docx) are now covered by the root
# allow-list above and no longer need naming.
#
# `data/_*` is one rule for the whole underscore-prefixed scratch family and
# replaces eight name-specific ones (_weekly_skeleton_*.md, _braze_docs_*,
# _bf/, _p2/, _bf_*.py, _p2_*.py, _session_*.py, _brief_*.md). Same reason the
# root became an allow-list: a rule that names one shape protects that shape and
# nothing else. Measured 2026-08-15 — within a day of the 08-14 repo cleanup the
# class had regrown to 18 untracked `data/_*` session scripts, and one
# (`_fix_daily_brief_counts_20260815.py`) was tracked and had reached the public
# mirror. Deliberate migrations keep their real names (`data/fix_*.sql`,
# `data/rollback_*.sql`) and stay tracked — the underscore IS the scratch marker.
data/_*
data/saeima_tmp/
data/saeima/
data/saeima_snapshots/
data/*.log
data/scratch_*

# Auth
data/x_cookies.json
data/x_cookies/

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Output
output/

# Visual Companion brainstorm mockups
.superpowers/

# Deploy creds
.env.deploy

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Archives
*.gz
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Debug / temp
.playwright-mcp/
.pytest_cache/
.tmp/
tmp/
tmp_*
.scratch/
.scratch_*
.git-commit-msg.tmp
logs/
videos/

# uv lockfile — project is not yet uv-managed (pyproject has no [project]/[tool.uv]).
# Remove this line when we actually adopt uv for dependency resolution.
uv.lock

# Screenshots (dev artifacts)
*.png
!docs/tweet_bank/**/*.png
# Brand assets — versionēti, lai svaigs klons/publiskais spogulis renderē pilnu vietni
!assets/og-image.png
!assets/favicon-*.png
!assets/apple-touch-icon.png

# Downloaded docs
*.pdf

# Claude Code config — agent prompts (.claude/agents/) ARE canonical and tracked;
# only per-operator runtime artefacts stay ignored
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
autoresearch-results.tsv

# Handoff archives (kept in working tree but not in git history)
atmina-handoff/
atmina-handoff.zip

# social agent draft images
data/social/drafts/*.png
data/x_cookies_atmina.json

# Local diagnostic artifacts (not shared)
data/autoresearch/

# Worktrees
.worktrees/

# Obsidian per-machine UI state (open-files list etc.) — churns on every vault
# browse; not content. The rest of wiki/.obsidian/ (config) stays tracked.
wiki/.obsidian/workspace.json

# --- Working-tree hygiene: scratch / binary / one-off, not for public repo ---
# NB: `docs/audits/` was listed here 2026-08-14 with the rationale "not for public
# repo" and REMOVED again 2026-08-22. The rationale was already satisfied elsewhere:
# `docs/audits` sits in the public-mirror exclusion set (docs/funding/repo-sync.md
# step 2), exactly like `docs/plans` — which is tracked AND mirror-excluded, 19/19.
# Untracking bought no privacy and cost provenance: `BACKLOG.md`'s ingestion contract
# (2026-08-19) routes investigation evidence to this directory, and by 2026-08-22
# three of the eight audit documents cited from tracked files were already gone —
# one `git clean` from a citation target. Audits are evidence; evidence gets versioned.
docs/brand/
docs/featured-images/
# tweet_bank: keep .md drafts + *-thread-prompts.json; exclude binaries / renders / image dirs
docs/tweet_bank/*.docx
docs/tweet_bank/*.html
docs/tweet_bank/*.png
docs/tweet_bank/*-images/
docs/tweet_bank/2026-05-16-1286-valodas-balsojums/
# synthesis: keep the hand-written .md source (wiki/synthesis/); exclude the print
# intermediates. `render_synthesis_pdf.py` writes a base64-inlined .html next to the
# .pdf; the .pdf was always ignored (*.pdf) but the .html was tracked and shipped to
# the PUBLIC mirror at 2 836 294 B — 9,96 % of the whole 28,48 MB public tree for a
# file nothing reads (the published page is output/atmina/sintezes/*.html, ~29 KB,
# rendered independently from the .md). Regenerable; untracked 2026-08-22.
docs/synthesis/*.html
# NB: eleven name-specific `scripts/*.py` deny rules + `scripts/_scratch/` were
# deleted here 2026-08-15 — verified: none of the twelve paths existed any more
# (the files went in the 08-14 cleanup, the rules stayed). A deny rule for a
# file that does not exist protects nothing and reads as if it does.
wiki/dailies/

# Ielādes žurnāls — append-only operatora diagnostika, kas rotē reizi mēnesī
# (~110 KB/mēn). To lasa `read_ingest_log()` no DISKA, interaktīvi; neviens
# automātisks ceļš to neizsauc, un jēgpilnā vēsture dzīvo wiki/CHANGELOG.md.
# Indekss `wiki/log-ingest.md` paliek izsekots — ignorēta ir tikai mape.
wiki/log-ingest/

# NVO dotāciju analīzes avoti (privāti: xlsx izvilkums + iekšējā piezīme;
# publiskā lapa dzīvo curated/atmina/analizes/)
data/NVO/
docs/eval/_run-*
